"""What the model declares, held to a committed capture of a real server.

It fails in one direction: an attribute that is declared, is in no captured
answer, and carries no reason it could not be observed. That is an invented
name, and whatever reads it is empty on every real server. The other direction
is reported and never failed: a server sends far more than a tool reads, and
the model declares what is read.

Run this file to print both directions. The standard library is all it needs.
"""

